-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/1c9890d1-4eda-5588-855f-3e26e595fb7e
-- title:
--   Semistable model with Igusa–Drinfeld components and henselian descent
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q\ge 5$ is a prime, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; write $k$ for `ResidueField A`. The ambient field is $F=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is `levelH q M'`, the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$). Beside it sits `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field; the hypothesis `hle` asserts that it is contained in $F$.
--
--   The further data are: a finite set $W$ of places (over $k$) of `modularFunctionFieldC k M'`, the subfield of $k((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j$ substituted $q\mapsto q^{M'}$, with `hW` saying that the members of $W$ are exactly the places in `ssPlaces q M' k`, that is the places $w$ which are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and for which `w.evalAt (jGeomGen k M')` lies in the supersingular set `ssJSet q k`; a constant reduction datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC k M')`, consisting of a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` from it onto `modularFunctionFieldC k M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places, and the compatibilities recorded in that structure (an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when it lies in $A$, the residue of the image of $a\in A$ is the image of the residue of $a$, every nonzero element has a scalar multiple with nonzero residue, and the place map preserves degrees and pushforwards of principal divisors); the hypothesis `hR₀`, which states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $k$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; an element $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$; an element $\zeta$ of `Idx q`, the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and two families of valuation subrings of $F$, namely `OIg` indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and `OSS` indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa group of hypotheses describes `OIg`. The hypothesis `hIg_inf` characterises the ring at `lineInfty q`, the class of $(1,0)$: an element $f\in F$ lies in `OIg (lineInfty q)` exactly when there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ to $k((q))$ is nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$. The hypothesis `hIg` asserts that for every $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ there is $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ` and `OIg ℓ` equal to the preimage of `OIg (lineInfty q)` under the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The hypothesis `hIg_inj` says `OIg` is injective, and `hIg_perm` that for every $\zeta'\in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ there is a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ with the preimage of `OIg ℓ` under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to `OIg (σ ℓ)` for all $\ell$.
--
--   The supersingular group of hypotheses describes `OSS`. By `hSS_A`, for each $s\in W$ an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `OSS s` (after mapping into $F$) precisely when it lies in $A$. By `hSS_over`, for each $s\in W$ and each $f\in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of the $q$-expansion $j$ has nonnegative order: if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $f$ in $F$ under the inclusion `hle` lies in `OSS s`, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value of $s$ at that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in `OSS s` and in the maximal ideal of `OSS s`. By `hSS_fix`, the preimage of `OSS s` under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` is `OSS s` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. By `hSS_tr`, for each $s\in W$ there is $t\in$ `OSS s` such that for every $a\in A$ the difference of $t$ and the image of $a$ lies in `OSS s` and is a unit there.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist a scheme $X$ in universe $0$, a morphism `toBase : X ⟶ Spec A`, together with the assertions that $X$ is integral and that `toBase` is proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, and a ring isomorphism $\varphi$ from $F$ onto `X.functionField`, such that the following hold.
--
--   First, $\varphi$ is compatible with the base: for every $a\in A$, the value of $\varphi$ at the image of $a$ in $F$ equals `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField toBase a`, the germ at the generic point of the global section of $\mathcal O_X$ obtained from $a$ through `toBase`.
--
--   Second, for every point $y$ of $X$ the stalk `X.presheaf.stalk y` is integrally closed.
--
--   Third, the model descends: there exist a subfield $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over $K_0$, a type $A_0$ carrying the structure of a commutative ring which is a domain, a discrete valuation ring and a henselian local ring, a local ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0\to A$, an element $\varpi_0\in A_0$, a scheme $X_0$ with a morphism `toBase₀ : X₀ ⟶ Spec A₀` such that $X_0$ is integral and `toBase₀` is proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, an isomorphism `iso` from $X$ to the pullback of `toBase₀` along `Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ι)`, a subfield $F_0\subseteq F$ with $F$ algebraic over $F_0$, and a ring isomorphism $\varphi_0$ from $F_0$ onto `X₀.functionField`, for which, writing $\mathrm{pr}$ for `iso.hom` followed by the first pullback projection: $\pi\in K_0$; the maximal ideal of $A_0$ is generated by $\varpi_0$; $\iota$ is injective; the image of $A_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A\cap K_0$; the residue map of $A$ composed with $\iota$ is surjective; `iso.hom` followed by the second pullback projection is `toBase`; $\mathrm{pr}$ carries the generic point of $X$ to the generic point of $X_0$; for every $s\in F_0$, $\varphi(s)$ is obtained from $\varphi_0(s)$ by the specialisation map of the structure sheaf of $X_0$ attached to that equality of generic points, followed by the stalk map of $\mathrm{pr}$ at the generic point of $X$; a point $x$ of $X$ lies in the smooth locus of `toBase` if and only if $\mathrm{pr}(x)$ lies in the smooth locus of `toBase₀`; and for every point $x_0$ of $X_0$ lying over the closed point of $A_0$ and outside the smooth locus of `toBase₀`, the stalk at $x_0$ is a noetherian ring and there is a natural number $w\ge 1$ such that $w$ is a unit in $A_0$ and there is a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $x_0$ with respect to its maximal ideal onto
--   $$\widehat{A_0}[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(X_0X_1-\varpi_0^{\,w}\big),$$
--   where $\widehat{A_0}$ is the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, such that $e$ carries, for each $a\in A_0$, the image in the completion of the germ at $x_0$ of the global section determined by $a$ to the class of the constant two-variable power series with value the image of $a$ in $\widehat{A_0}$.
--
--   Fourth, the special fibre is described by a dictionary of components and nodes: there exist maps $\mathrm{gen}$ from $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)\sqcup W$ to $X$ and $\mathrm{nd}$ from $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)\times W$ to $X$, both injective, such that for every $\ell$ the subring `SemistableModel.localRing X φ (gen (Sum.inl ℓ))` of $F$, namely the image under $\varphi^{-1}$ of the stalk at that point inside the function field, equals `OIg ℓ`; for every $s\in W$ the corresponding subring at $\mathrm{gen}(\mathrm{inr}\,s)$ equals `OSS s`; every point $\mathrm{gen}(i)$ lies over the closed point of $A$; a point $x$ of $X$ lying over the closed point of $A$ is of the form $\mathrm{gen}(i)$ if and only if $x$ specialises to some point distinct from $x$; each $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ is closed, in the sense that any $y$ to which $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ specialises equals $\mathrm{nd}(e)$; for $e=(\ell,s)$ and an index $i$, $\mathrm{gen}(i)$ specialises to $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ if and only if $i=\mathrm{inl}\,\ell$ or $i=\mathrm{inr}\,s$; no $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ lies in the smooth locus of `toBase`; every point of $X$ different from all $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ lies in the smooth locus of `toBase`; every closed point $x$ of the fibre over the closed point of $A$ which is not one of the $\mathrm{nd}(e)$ admits a unique index $i$ with $\mathrm{gen}(i)$ specialising to $x$; and finally, for every closed point $x$ of the fibre over the closed point of $A$ and every $a\in A$, either $j-a$ or $(j-a)^{-1}$ belongs to `SemistableModel.localRing X φ x`, where $j$ denotes the image in $F$ under the inclusion `hle` of the element `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $q$-expansion of the modular function $j$ with coefficients in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   This is the construction, in the language of schemes, of a normal semistable proper flat model over $\operatorname{Spec}A$ of the modular curve whose function field is `fieldBar q M'`, with the Igusa components pinned to the given valuation subrings `OIg` indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$, the supersingular components pinned to `OSS` indexed by the supersingular places $W$, the nodes indexed by pairs, the thicknesses of the nodes tame on a henselian discrete valuation subbase, and a dichotomy for $j$ at closed points of the special fibre. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.SemistableCovering.exists_semistableModel_descent_of_discCharts_of_noCuspFreePackageSS_of_jPins_of_nodeRings_nodeCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.SemistableCovering.exists_semistableModel_descent_of_discCharts_of_noCuspFreePackageSS_of_jPins_of_nodeRings_nodeCharts), which packages the resulting model as semistable covering data for the level-lowering argument.
